   "response_text": "**Fixed.** Only `invkit/parsing.py` changed \u2014 no test files touched.\n\nThe bug: `_to_int` / `_to_float` just called `int()`/`float()` on the raw field, so `\"1,200\"` and `\"1,299.50\"` blew up.\n\nThe fix (DRY, one helper):\n- Added `_unseparate(raw)` which strips thousands separators **only when they're correctly grouped** (`^[+-]?\\d{1,3}(?:,\\d{3})+(?:\\.\\d+)?$`). So `1,200` \u2192 `1200`, `1,299.50` \u2192 `1299.50`, but junk like `1,23` still raises.\n- `_to_int` and `_to_float` both route through it, keeping the existing behavior otherwise.\n\nVerified:\n- Quoted `1,200` / `1,299.50` parse to `1200` / `1299.5` \u2705\n- Plain numbers unaffected \u2705\n- Non-numeric values still raise `ParseError` with the right `line_no` (2) \u2705\n- Mis-grouped separators rejected \u2705\n- Negative price **and** negative quantity still rejected (checked even via `-1,200`) \u2705\n- `pytest`: 4 passed \ud83d\udc36\n\nDONE",
